From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anthony Fu <github@antfu.me>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:30:10 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] feat(app): pick a host icon and show it in host pickers

A host could only be told apart by its name and its color, and the color
only showed in sidebar badges. Host appearance now has an icon too, picked
next to the color in the host's settings. Badges draw it, and every host
list (host pickers, the sidebar's host filter, the settings host switcher
and Add project's host step) draws the host's icon in its color. The
status dot sits on the icon's bottom-right corner only while the host is
not connected.

The icon is per-device, like the color, and saved under its own storage
key (@paseo:host-icons), not in the host registry. The registry schema is
strict and a registry that fails it is deleted whole, so an icon field
there would cost every saved host on a build without it. Registries that
an earlier version of this change wrote an icon into still parse, and
their icons move to the new key when the registry loads.

Fork-Change: F-9
